.TH COF-INIT 1 "2026-11-13" "cof 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cof-init \- Initialize a new circuitry project in the current directory
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
cof init [OPTIONS]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Initializes a new Circuitry project in the current directory: a starter config
and example orchestration.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --yes, -y
Non-interactive: accept defaults (or --adapter/--adapter-url/--model) without
prompting.
.TP
.B --adapter
ADAPTER Adapter to configure (default: ollama).
.TP
.B --adapter-url
ADAPTER_URL Adapter base URL (default: http://localhost:11434).
.TP
.B --model
MODEL Default model (default: llama3.1:8b).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B cof init
Scaffolds a new project in the current directory.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The command failed, or the input was invalid.
.TP
.B 2
A usage error -- an unrecognized option or missing argument.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBcof(1)\fR, \fBcof-setup(1)\fR
